K.12 Reading the diagrams together

The diagrams are arranged so that the mathematical core of the theory can be checked without reading the proofs:

· K.1 and K.2 establish that the correctability object is a partial order, and that the count is a stipulation rather than a measurement.
· K.3 establishes that exit capacity is a bottleneck, and that the two-of-three rule is inconsistent with non-compensation.
· K.4 establishes that the accumulation claim is a signed interaction estimand, not a metaphor.
· K.5 establishes that the four reversibility levels are nested, and that the conjunction collapses to exercisability.
· K.6 and K.8 establish that Theorems 1 and 3 are consequences of the Markov condition and the backdoor criterion respectively, and that the theorems are false if those conditions are violated.
· K.7, K.9, and K.10 establish that the framework's three directed structures and its admissibility filter are distinct objects, and that conflating them is the source of the errors the present version corrects.
· K.11 is the composite object that the empirical work of H1–H7 must measure.

